"9" page="108" id="N0x3480230N0x2f0c1f0" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="17666116" ext-link-type="pubmed"/></article-meta></front><body><sec><title/><p>Due to an oversight, the author of the above article [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B1">1</xref>] was incorrectly listed as having no competing interests. The competing interests section of this article should have read:</p></sec><sec><title>Competing interests</title><p>GC has served as an expert witness for plaintiff lawyers preparing hormone therapy litigation. GC has received research support from GlaxoSmithKline, from the American Cancer Society, and from the Breast Cancer Research Foundation. No group or organization funded this manuscript.</p></sec></body><back><ref-list><ref id="B1"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Colditz</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Decline in breast cancer incidence due to removal of promoter: combination estrogen plus progestin</article-title><source>Breast Cancer Research</source><year>2007</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>108</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17666116</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/bcr1736</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>